<title>UK: Aluminium stocks fell in November - IPAI.</title>
<headline>Aluminium stocks fell in November - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total stocks of all forms of aluminium at Western world smelters excluding finished end-products, fell to 3.090 million tonnes at the end of November 1996, compared with 3.161 million in October and 3.506 million in November 1995, provisional International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) figures show.</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks fell to 1.653 million tonnes versus 1.686 million and 1.930 million, respectively.  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of the total aluminium stocks was as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			    Nov 96   Oct 96    Nov 95</p>
<p>    Africa		    63	 70	  79</p>
<p>    North America	1,455    1,495     1,602</p>
<p>    Latin America	  174	163	 182</p>
<p>    East/South Asia	174	165	 152</p>
<p>    Europe		 1,085    1,119     1,326</p>
<p>    Oceania		  139	149	 165</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks were distributed as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			   Nov 96    Oct 96    Nov 95</p>
<p>    Africa		   18	  24	  32</p>
<p>    North America	 662	 679	 757</p>
<p>    Latin America	 128	 119	 140</p>
<p>    East/South Asia     150	 139	 126</p>
<p>    Europe		  591	 611	 760</p>
<p>    Oceania		 104	 114	 115</p>
</text>
